# The Luvo web app.
#
# Copy to `.env.local`. Everything here is NEXT_PUBLIC_* and therefore inlined
# into the browser bundle at build time — nothing secret may be added to this
# file. Clerk's secret key and Stripe's live key belong in the deployment's own
# environment and are read only inside a route handler.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The Luvo API. Everything real comes from here: the catalogue, the renders, the
# generation queue, the credit ledger.
#
# Locally, run the whole backend in memory from the repo root — `npm run sandbox`
# — which serves on :8099 with no Railway, no R2 and no fal, and therefore no way
# to spend money. See docs/sandbox.md.
#
# With this unset the site still builds and every page still renders, but there
# is no catalogue and nothing can be generated. The footer says so rather than
# showing an empty grid with no explanation.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8099

# This site's own origin. Used for canonical links, Open Graph tags, the sitemap
# and the share fallback url. No trailing slash.
#
# On Vercel this falls back to the deployment's own URL, so a preview branch does
# not advertise production's canonical.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not implemented yet
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Both of these are read only to decide whether to say "coming soon". Setting one
# does not switch the feature on — the integration is not written. They are here
# so the seam is visible rather than surprising.

# Clerk, for sign-in. An account exists for exactly one reason: so purchased
# credits survive a browser. When this lands, the flow is a route handler that
# exchanges a Clerk session for `POST /v1/account/sign-in` and adopts this
# browser's device secret — the server already does that for Apple and Google.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Stripe, for checkout. Note that `credit_products` has no price column and the
# API never sends one: the Price object is the authority. `web/lib/pricing.ts`
# holds indicative figures until then and is deleted when this is wired.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
